know, and we covered it.

00:00:09.981 --> 00:00:14.650
Earlier today, Donald Trump was caught on
an audio recording of a phone call with the

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:19.230
Georgia secretary of state asking them to
find him.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:23.510
Eleven thousand seven hundred and eighty votes,
which would give him a win in Georgia over

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:24.510
Joe Biden.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.420
Now, even if they did that, it wouldn't flip
the results of the election because Joe Biden

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.310
won enough other states to win anyway.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:36.420
But this caller points out something sort
of tongue in cheek but that we are hearing

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.050
who recorded the call.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.039
It was illegal to record the call.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.039
That's the focus.

00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:42.039
Take a listen.

00:00:42.039 --> 00:00:43.039
Hi, David.

00:00:43.039 --> 00:00:45.520
So, yeah, everyone's talking about this phone
call, and I just want to say I think it was

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.520
absolutely perfect.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.359
There was absolutely it was a perfect phone
call.

00:00:50.359 --> 00:00:53.460
There was nothing wrong with it.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.460
Perfect.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:00.499
There should be doing some investigations
for illegally recording it, right?

00:01:00.499 --> 00:01:05.129
Yeah, illegally recording a private phone
call is just.

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:06.129
Yeah.

00:01:06.129 --> 00:01:12.130
So I get that they're joking, but there's
a few things here to talk about, number one,

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:16.850
both side, you know that I don't both sides,
almost anything.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:23.040
Both sides mostly play this game when there
is a leak and they like the content of the

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.040
leak.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.649
They focus on the content and they ignore
how it was obtained.

00:01:26.649 --> 00:01:31.079
When they don't like the content of the leak,
they say, whoa, hold on a second, that was

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:37.009
illegally recorded or it was leaked by someone
who didn't have access to it or whatever.

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:41.479
Democrats and Republicans really both do this
almost to the same degree.

00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:44.869
And it's one of the areas where there really
is very little difference between Democrats

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:45.950
and Republicans.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:51.250
However, what is interesting is that presumably
Donald Trump well, we know Donald Trump was

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:56.249
in Washington, D.C. when this call was made
and Brad Raffensperger was in Georgia when

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.759
this call was made.

00:01:57.759 --> 00:02:04.579
Both Georgia and D.C. are to our one party
consent territories, meaning it is legal to

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:09.830
record a phone call as long as someone on
the call knows that it's being recorded.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:16.160
The question is, if the people who were doing
the recording and knew it was being recorded

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.120
were in Georgia and no one in D.C. knew it.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.790
I am not a lawyer, as many of you know.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:29.360
My question would be, does D.C. law about
one party consent mean that at least one party

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.950
in D.C. needs to know that it's being recorded
for it to be legal?

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.970
I don't know the answer to that.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:39.450
And these one party versus two party consent
things, when you have different laws in different

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:45.170
states, when the two states on a call have
different laws, this becomes a federal issue.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:50.690
And anyway, it's kind of a whole bigger topic,
but it may not actually have been an illegal

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:51.840
recording here.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.470
It's quite possible because both territories
are one party consent that this was actually

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:02.640
perfectly legal to record, assuming some of
the parties on the call were the ones doing

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.640
the recording.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.240
We don't have that information yet.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:11.770
I am sure that one of the many lawyers in
the audience will clarify this for me.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:15.960
But yes, we should be outraged.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.570
Not that Trump is openly pressuring people
to steal the election.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.300
We should be outraged that this was recorded.

